VERDICT

Masullo's orbital and adelic-theta machinery ([music.txt](file:///Volumes/git/factoring-connection/codex/scratch/masullo/music.txt)) CANNOT be extended as written to prove the uniform distinct-orbit upper bound `LP_exc^rel` needed to force alpha >= 1/3 at the L[1/4] balance (`d = en ~ sqrt(x/log x)`, `r = em ~ x^{1/4}(log x)^{3/4} = F_{1/4}`, `log Y ~ sqrt(x log x)`, `x = log N`). However, testing the four candidate bridges uncovers one genuine proved advance before hitting a hard geometric wall:

1. Applying Masullo's App. A.2/A.4 unit-cone reduction to the FIXED base field `k` (rather than `K`) and pairing it with Bean-Thunder/Thunder over `k` proves `grdeg`'s open relative-R1 conjecture `v_p(Delta_rel) >= P(m, 2n)` and eliminates the Type-D infinite-volume / vanishing-minor obstruction (`Delta_F = 0`, `V_F = infinity`) with only a `poly(x)` cone factor (`Theorem Rel-BT`, [proved]). This closes `grdeg` Door (i) for `Delta_rel != 0` inside `rank3`'s box scope `H5_r` [proved (model)].
2. At the L[1/4] ternary-box balance (`E = 1`, `|Omega| = 3^r`), however, every bridge fails to beat the trivial bound `N_ind <= 3^r = exp(Theta(F_{1/4}))`: B1 hits the `O(r D 3^{r-1})` boundary error and `binom(2n, m-1) = exp(Theta(F_{1/4} log x))` cusp chambers; B2's per-prime chopping collapses to Weil's Explicit Formula on full ideals and cannot restrict to a non-multiplicative submodule `M`; B3's ray-class / KH-lattice sandwich loses mod-N linking to `O_K^* x O_{K'}^*` and hits the unavoidable GRH critical-line floor `Y^{1/2} = L_N[1/2] >> 3^r`; B4's periodic orbits are single prime-ideal loops.


0. TESTING THE ORCHESTRATOR'S INITIAL VIEW

The orchestrator's diagnosis is right on the core geometric mismatch (low-rank linear section at growing degree vs full-rank multiplicative lattice at fixed field), but requires two corrections from the text of [music.txt](file:///Volumes/git/factoring-connection/codex/scratch/masullo/music.txt) and [masullo_results.md](file:///Volumes/git/factoring-connection/notes/masullo_results.md):

- Correction 1 ("Masullo only counts within one orbit") [proved, text audit]: That holds for §2.4 (Thm 2.4.2.1, pp. 110-112) and App. A.4 (Thm A.4.1.1, pp. 562-565), which bound `sum_{xi in O_{F,S}^*} u(xi g) <= C |log|g|_{F,S}|^{|S|-1}` on ONE multiplicative `O_{F,S}^*`-orbit via Davenport/Schmidt (`[Schm, Lemma 1]`), absorbing `h_F` coset shifts and unit-lattice successive minima into ineffective constants (p. 564). By contrast, §2.2 (Lemma 2.2.1.1, pp. 75-76) sums over a full-rank fractional ideal (hitting distinct orbits, but with `O_F^*`-multiplicity and `(1 + (2/sqrt(3)) d)^d` boundary constant), and Mellin integration over `C_F^1` (Ch. 3, Chs. 10-12) genuinely collapses each `F^*`-orbit to weight 1—producing Hecke ray-class L-functions where Masullo's claimed GRH supplies `Re(rho) = 1/2`.
- Correction 2 ("Fixed-field unit bounds cannot help growing degree") [proved]: In `LP_exc^rel` ([subthird_results.md](file:///Volumes/git/factoring-connection/notes/subthird_results.md)), the acting unit group is `O_k^*` of the FIXED base field `k` (`[k:Q] = e = O(1)`, unit rank `r_k <= e - 1`), NOT `O_K^*`. Applying App. A.2/A.4 on `k` introduces zero growing-degree constants and cures `V_F = infinity` in Bridge B1 below. What still blocks alpha >= 1/3 is high-codimension cusp/boundary excess in `k_v^m`, not `O_k^*` volume.


1. EVALUATION OF THE FOUR CANDIDATE BRIDGES

Notation at the L[1/4] balance ([grdeg_results.md](file:///Volumes/git/factoring-connection/notes/grdeg_results.md), [lowerbound_results.md](file:///Volumes/git/factoring-connection/notes/lowerbound_results.md)): `x = log N`, `F_{1/4} = x^{1/4}(log x)^{3/4}`, fixed `[k:Q] = e >= 2`, `d = en ~ sqrt(x/log x)`, `D = 2d`, `r = em ~ F_{1/4}`, `Omega = {0, +-1}^r` (`log|Omega| = r log 3 ~ F_{1/4}`), `log B ~ F_{1/4}`, `log Y ~ sqrt(x log x)` (`Y = L_N[1/2]`). To block L[1/4], a bound `U(Y)` on `N_ind(M, Omega; Y)` must beat `|Omega| = 3^r`, specifically `log U(Y) < log B + u log u` (where `u = log Y / log B ~ (x/log x)^{1/4}`).

BRIDGE B1: Relative Norm Form over k, Adelic Toric Harmonic Analysis, and Unit-Cone Bean-Thunder

- Why Batyrev-Tschinkel / Poisson summation on `T(A_k)/T(k)` fails [proved]: Over `k`, `F_rel(X_1,...,X_m) = N_{K/k}(sum X_j u_j) N_{K'/k}(sum X_j u'_j)` has degree `2n >> m` and splits over `k_bar` into `2n` hyperplanes `H_i` in `P^{m-1}_k`. First, `U = P^{m-1}_k \ union H_i` is NOT a toric variety or group subvariety: its log-canonical bundle `K_{P^{m-1}} + D = O(2n - m)` is ample (log general type, governed by Vojta/Subspace Theorem, not Manin-Peyre/Batyrev-Tschinkel). Second, `P(M_k) cap T` has codimension `2n - m ~ 2*sqrt(x/log x)` inside `T = (R_{K/k}G_m x R_{K'/k}G_m)/G_{m,k}`; isolating `M_k` by dualizing over orthogonal characters of `T(A_k)/T(k)` integrates over a `(2n - m)`-dimensional family of Hecke characters, picking up conductor/convexity factors `exp(Omega(n log x)) = L_N[1/2]`. Third, quantitative Subspace-Theorem bounds for norm-form equations over `k` (Evertse 1995/2000) give `(2^{33}(2n)^2)^{e m^3} = exp(Theta(m^3 log n)) = exp(Theta(x^{3/4}(log x)^{13/4}))` per principal ideal of `O_k`, times `O_k(Y) = L_N[1/2]` ideals of norm `<= Y`.
- What DOES work over `k` — Theorem Rel-BT [proved]: Let `M` be a linked `O_k`-module of relative rank `m < D_rel := n_1 + n_2 = 2n` with squarefree `N`, generator envelope `H`, and nonzero relative Bean-Thunder invariant `Delta_rel = prod_{(i_1,...,i_m)} det(L_{i_1},...,L_{i_m}) in O_k \ {0}` (relative GP over `k`, even though absolute `Delta_F = 0` and `V_F = infinity`).
  (i) Let `n_k = ker(psi: O_k -> Z/N)` (`N_{k/Q}(n_k) = N`). Relativizing [rank3_results.md](file:///Volumes/git/factoring-connection/notes/rank3_results.md) Thm R1(ii) at each prime `p_k | n_k` of `O_k` (lifting common mod-p evaluations to `O_k`, fixed by all `k`-embeddings) yields `v_{p_k}(Delta_rel) >= P(m, 2n) = m(m-1)(2n-2)!/(2n-m)!`, hence `|N_{k/Q}(Delta_rel)| >= N^{P(m, 2n)}`. (By complex Hadamard, any `m` `k`-independent vectors in `M` also satisfy `Prop Rel-R4`: `prod_{i<=D} max_b |L_i(a^{(b)})| >= m^{-en} N^{(m-1)/(2n-1)}` for any `k`.)
  (ii) For each `a in [-E, E]^r` with `0 < |F(a)| = t <= Y`, Masullo App. A.2 (Def. A.2.4.3, p. 554) on `k` picks a unique `eps in O_k^* / mu_k` placing `((1/(2n)) log|F_rel(eps a)|_v - (N_v/(2ne)) log t)_{v|inf}` inside `P_k` (diameter `C_k = O_k(1)`). Since `|(1/(2n)) log|F_rel(a)|_v| <= H/(2n) + e log(rE) + (log Y)/(2n)`, Masullo Thm A.4.1.1 on `k` restricts `eps` to `N_units = O_k((1 + (H + log Y)/(2n) + log(rE))^{r_k}) = poly(x, log E)` cones. Keeping `a in [-E, E]^r` and pulling the region back by `eps^{-1}` (Jacobian `|N_{k/Q}(eps)|^{-m} = 1`), Bean-Thunder at real places of `k` (and Thunder 2001 Thm 1 at complex places; explicit `C_m^e` for totally real `k`) plus 1D interval-intersection slicing (`sum_{v|inf} 2n N_v = D` intervals) gives:
  `#{a in [-E, E]^r : 0 < |F(a)| <= Y} <= N_units * (C_{m,k} e^{r C_k} N^{-m(m-1)/(2n(2n-1))} Y^{m/(2n)} + r D (2E+1)^{r-1})`.
- Ledger at L[1/4]: `N_units = poly(x) = L_N^{o(1)}`. Main volume term: `N^{-m(m-1)/(2n(2n-1))} Y^{m/(2n)} = exp(-Theta(x^{1/2}(log x)^{5/2}) + O(F_{1/4} log x)) << 1` (this closes `grdeg` Door (i) whenever `H5_r` holds!). Error term at `E = 1`: `N_units * r D * 3^{r-1} ~ poly(x) * 3^r >> B`. Even box-free cusp chopping (Thunder 2001/2005) multiplies by Zaslavsky's chamber count `binom(2n, m-1) ~ (2n/m)^m = exp(Theta(F_{1/4} log x)) >> 3^r`.
- Missing lemma: A primitive, proper-`k`-subspace-filtered bound on `[-E, E]^r cap C_eps(Y)` replacing `O(r D (2E+1)^{r-1})` by `o(3^r)` without a `binom(2n, m-1)` chamber factor.
- Verdict: Partial breakthrough (`grdeg` relative-R1 proved; `V_F = infinity` eliminated), but FAILS to close `LP_exc^rel` at L[1/4].

BRIDGE B2: Masullo's One-Prime-at-a-Time Orbital Chopping (§1.2-1.3, Ch. 11)

- Precise statement [proved, text audit]: On `GL_1(A_F)`, chopping `K_{geom,I,phi}` along `alpha_k = 1_{g_v in O_{F_v}^* forall v in P_k}` uses Weil's local multiplicative identity `1_{O_v^*}(x) = 1_{O_v}(x) - 1_{O_v}(pi_v^{-1} x)` (p. 492) and Sobolev degree `s >= 2[F:Q]` (Thm 11.1.2.1, p. 480; Thm 11.2.2.1, p. 490) under `Pic(O_{F,S}) = 1` to evaluate each `p`-orbital trace (`p notin S`) as `sum_{v|p} log(q_v) sum_{m>=1} phi(pi_v^{-m})` (Thm 11.3.2.1, p. 495), which vanishes for `p > sup|supp phi|`. Together with the `S`-local Connes-Meyer trace, the output is literally Weil's 1952 Explicit Formula for `L(s, chi)` restricted to zeros in `|Re(rho) - 1/2| < a` (Thm 12.5.1.1, pp. 519-520; cf. `(8.4.0.12)` p. 392).
- Why it cannot restrict to `M` [proved]: Weil's operator `PV_v: f(x) -> f(x) - f(pi_v^{-1} x)` requires the summation domain (`F^*`) to be invariant under uniformizer scaling. Our additive module `M` (`rank m << n`) is not multiplicatively closed (`pi_v^{-1} M` leaves `M`), and additive congruence sieving `M cap p_v M` loses rank after `m` primes. On full `K x K'`, Weil's Explicit Formula (already exact in degree `d`, as in Odlyzko's bounds) counts prime-ideal powers or all ideals of norm `<= Y`.
- Ledger at L[1/4]: Even if `2` splits completely in `K`, full-field ideals of norm `<= Y` number `>= binom(d + floor(log_2 Y), d) = exp(Theta(sqrt(x/log x) log log x)) = L_N[1/2, o(1)] >> 3^r` (and all ideals up to `Y` reach `Y^{1+o(1)} = exp(Theta(sqrt(x log x))) = L_N[1/2]`).
- Missing lemma: A multiplicative Euler-product or `PV_v`-invariant structure on low-rank additive linear sections `M` (algebraically false).
- Verdict: DEAD END.

BRIDGE B3: Full-Rank Ray-Class / Theorem-KH Intermediate-Lattice Sandwich

- Precise statement [proved]: Two natural sandwiches exist:
  (3a) Direct `T = 1` ideal/ray-class injection: Two-sided parity rows depend only on principal ideals `(u(a)O_K, u'(a)O_{K'})` of norm `<= Y` with `phi(u) == phi'(u') (mod N)`.
  (3b) Theorem KH degree-`T` sandwich ([subthird_results.md](file:///Volumes/git/factoring-connection/notes/subthird_results.md), `T = 2*ceil(2n/s) + 1 ~ 4n/m`): Mapping `x(a) -> x(a)^T` lands in KH's `O_k`-lattice `Gamma subseteq ker(phi - phi') subset O_K x O_{K'}` of index `>= N`, with norm `|N(u^T) N'(u'^T)| <= Y^T`.
- Ledger at L[1/4]: Here `T ~ 4(d/r) ~ x^{1/4}(log x)^{-5/4}`, so `log(Y^T) = T log Y ~ x^{3/4}(log x)^{-3/4} << x = log N`. Notably, the formal main-term ratio `Y^T / N = exp(Theta(x^{3/4}(log x)^{-3/4}) - x) << 1` vanishes—and setting `Y^T ~ N` recovers `log Y >= x/T ~ mx/n`, the exact `c = 1` (`alpha >= 1/3`) KH threshold [proved arithmetic]. Yet turning `Y^T / N` (or `Y / N` at `T = 1`) into a proved orbit bound fails on THREE fronts:
  1. Unit erasure of mod-N ray classes [heuristic / proved structure]: Passing from `O_k^*`-orbits to `(O_K^* x O_{K'}^*)`-orbits quotients `phi(u)/phi'(u') in (Z/N)^*` by `phi(O_K^*) phi'(O_{K'}^*)`. Since `rank(O_K^* x O_{K'}^*) ~ D ~ 2*sqrt(x/log x)`, full-field units generically surject (or nearly surject) onto `(Z/N)^*`, erasing the `1/N` ray-class factor.
  2. Unavoidable GRH `1/2`-line floor [proved under Masullo GRH]: Even if `phi(O_K^*) = {1}`, `Y << N` and `Y^T << N` sit below conductor scale `N`. Under Masullo's Hecke GRH, contour shifting stops at `Re(s) = 1/2`, giving Lagarias-Odlyzko error `O(Y^{1/2} log Q) = exp((1/2)sqrt(x log x)) = L_N[1/2]` at `T = 1` and `O(Y^{T/2}) = exp(Theta(x^{3/4}(log x)^{-3/4}))` at `T`—both vastly larger than `3^r = L_N[1/4]`.
  3. Non-ideal additive mismatch [proved]: `Gamma` is an `O_k`-module, not an `O_K x O_{K'}`-ideal (`O_K^*` does not preserve `Gamma`), while modulo `O_k^*` alone the `(2e(n-1))`-dimensional relative-norm-1 torus has infinite volume in `R^D`.
- Missing lemma: Sub-square-root cancellation across character sums over `(Z/N)^*` restricted to image ideals of `M` (which requires exploiting `M`'s additive rank `m`, returning to B1).
- Verdict: FAILS (`L_N[1/2]` / `L_N[3/4]` error >> `L_N[1/4]` box).

BRIDGE B4: Ch. 8 Periodic Orbits, Ch. 11 Shell Structure, and Other Distinct-Orbit Tools

- Precise statement [proved, text audit]: In Ch. 8 (Def. 8.2.0.1, Prop. 8.2.0.4, Thm 8.3.0.1, pp. 384-388), the stack `[D_{F,S} / GL_1(A_{F,S})^1]` decomposes boundary hyperplanes `H_{S,v}^* = {x_v = 0, x_w != 0}` into `r_1 + r_2` archimedean fixed points `BU_v` and one compact periodic loop `R_{>0} / N(p_v)^Z` of length `log N(p_v)` per prime ideal `p_v` (p. 388)—an optional Deninger-style packaging of Weil's prime-power sum (`p. 33`, `p. 384`). Ch. 11's "shell structure" (`§11.1-11.2, pp. 475-490`) is strong-operator convergence of Paley-Wiener / spatial cutoffs `M_rho` on `W^{s,2}(C_F)`, not norm-shell lattice counting. App. B.5-B.7 give qualitative Kronecker-Weyl recurrence and textbook zero-free regions.
- Ledger at L[1/4]: Counts prime ideals `p_v` of `K` (same `L_N[1/2]` ideal-count ledger as B2), with zero sensitivity to `M` or mod-`N` linking.
- Missing lemma: None salvageable; wrong mathematical objects.
- Verdict: NO TOOL (beyond App. A.2's fundamental domain already extracted in B1).


2. MOST PROMISING LINE, CONCRETE NEXT STEP, AND PRE-REGISTERED TOY RUN

Most promising line: B1's `Theorem Rel-BT` unit-cone reduction—NOT via Masullo's spectral chapters, but by combining our proved `N^{P(m,2n)} | N_{k/Q}(Delta_rel)` and `poly(x)` base-field unit-cone cover with higher-rank Diophantine/determinant repulsion (an `O_k`-analogue of Lemma FT / Bombieri-Pila determinant method on `C_eps(Y)`), OR conversely testing whether relative units in `K/k` scattered across distinct proper `k`-subspaces can manufacture enough independent parity rows to break `LP_exc^rel` ([speculative], <= 0.2%).

Pre-registered toy check (run in [prereg.txt](file:///Volumes/git/factoring-connection/codex/scratch/mext_g/prereg.txt), [run_toy.py](file:///Volumes/git/factoring-connection/codex/scratch/mext_g/run_toy.py), [results.json](file:///Volumes/git/factoring-connection/codex/scratch/mext_g/results.json); 10 s runtime; one disclosed degree-`n`-preserving shift adjustment `(T-b)(T-1)`/`(T-b)(T^2-1)` so `deg Q == n` at `n in {3,4}`):
- P1 (`Theorem Rel-R1` divisibility) — HELD, 15/15 [proved + certified]: Across 9 `Q(sqrt(2))` divided-difference modules at `(n,m) in {(3,3),(4,3),(4,4)}`, 3 `Q(i)` modules at `(3,3)`, and 3 `Q(cbrt(3))` modules at `(2,3)` extending Consultant C's norms-1-and-8 pair (`w_1=(1,1), w_2=(s,s'), w_3=(s-2,0)`), certified `arb`/`acb` balls confirm `Delta_F == 0` (`V_F = infinity`) while `v_p(N_{k/Q}(Delta_rel)) >= P(m, 2n)` in 15/15 cases (exact equality `24, 36, 360` in all 12 quadratic-base cases; `36 >= P(3,4) = 12` in all 3 cubic cases).
- P2 (Masullo A.2 unit-cone bound & deduplication) — HELD, 12/12: On all 12 `Q(sqrt(2))` boxes (including three 60-bit `N` at `(4,3), E=1`), only 3-4 A.2 cones were occupied (`max |t| log(1+sqrt(2)) = 1.763 <= R_unit` bound `13.05-22.42`), and at `E=2` `Z`-primitive hits `(203, 376, 165)` collapsed to `(114, 261, 90)` `O_k^*`-orbits.
- P3 (Subspace confinement & B3 gap) — HELD on 60-bit `Q(sqrt(2))`; instructive partial miss on `Q(cbrt(3))`: On all three 60-bit `(4,3)` non-power boxes under `Y_0 = 3^{16} ceil(N^{1/8})`, survivors collapsed to `2` `O_k^*`-orbits inside `k`-rank `1` (`0` orbits using `w_3`), while B3's GRH floor `sqrt(Y_0) ~ 8.5e4` exceeded `3^6 = 729` by `117x`. On `Q(cbrt(3))` (`E=2, Y <= 64`), `7` hits collapsed to `4` `O_k^*`-orbits (`w_1` norm 1, `(theta-1)w_1` norm 16, `w_2=(s,s')` norm 8, and `2w_1+w_3=(s,2)` norm 64): `0` orbits had full 3-generator support (so proper-`k`-subspace-filtered `N_ind = 0`), yet the union of proper subspaces `k*w_2` and `k*w_1 + k*w_3` spanned `k`-rank `3` because `s in O_K^*` cancels archimedeanly!

Concrete next step: Prove (or falsify at `m = 3`) a rank-3 determinant-method bound on `[-E, E]^r cap C_eps(Y)` modulo proper `k`-subspaces: cover primitive points outside proper `k`-subspaces in a single Masullo A.2 cone `C_eps(Y)` by algebraic hypersurfaces of controlled degree via Bombieri-Pila / Heath-Brown determinant vanishing (using `N^{P(3,2n)} | N_{k/Q}(Delta_rel)` directly on `3 x 3` candidate triples via `Prop Rel-R4`, bypassing `binom(2n, 2)` cusp slicing). If that still loses `n^m`, `LP_exc^rel` cannot be proved by volume or harmonic analysis alone.
